 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Of course. Make sure he has a comfortable seat, a familiar face near the door, and snacks. Keep him engaged with things he still knows, like old songs or games. Keep things simple and don't try to correct him. Explain where things are slowly, and don't get upset if he forgets. People with dementia often feel anxious, and reassurance helps. If he' calm and doesn't feel rushed, yes. But only if they' safe and boring for him, like a museum with big glass boxes. Take breaks, and don't try do everything at once. Your dad will appreciate you being patient with him.",
